[size=6][b]SkyRT - hardware ray tracing for Sky: Children of the Light[/b][/size]

[b]The first public mod that brings real RTX ray tracing to Sky.[/b] Not a ReShade preset: SkyRT is a Vulkan layer that rebuilds the scene as acceleration structures and traces rays against the real geometry with hardware [i]ray_query[/i].

[size=5][b]What you get[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Ray-traced sun shadows[/b] with a soft penumbra, including shadows from things that are off screen or behind walls
[*][b]Characters cast smooth moving shadows[/b] (rebuilt every frame)
[*][b]Ray-traced ambient occlusion[/b] and one-bounce [b]global illumination[/b] with colour bleeding
[*][b]Denoising[/b]: bilateral blur + temporal accumulation
[*][b]16x anisotropic filtering[/b] for sharper textures at a distance
[*]The sun direction is read from the game
[*]No game files are modified
[/list]

[size=5][b]Not done yet[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Water and reflections
[*]Grass / foliage in the acceleration structure
[*]Light from fires and emissive objects, multi-bounce GI
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
Windows 10/11, GPU with Vulkan ray_query support, up-to-date drivers. Tested only on an RTX 5070 Ti.

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Unpack the archive anywhere
[*]Run [b]SkyRT_Panel.exe[/b] -> tab Game -> [b]Install ray tracing[/b] (no admin rights needed)
[*]Set the path to Sky.exe and press [b]Play with rays[/b]
[/list]
The panel also has presets and sliders for every setting (applied live) and a log viewer. In game: [b]Ctrl+Home[/b] = RT on/off, [b]Ctrl+End[/b] = debug views.

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Panel -> Uninstall.

[size=5][b]Notes[/b][/size]
Experimental. Unofficial fan project, not affiliated with thatgamecompany; it only hooks the graphics API on your PC. Use at your own risk. Source code (MIT): https://github.com/sstalkerr31-ai/Sky-RTX
